    "done_when": "The node's evidence fragment holds one table row for each binding sentence in skills/reckon-build/SKILL.md, and no other file. Method: a binding sentence states a rule a coordinator or worker must follow; it contains or implies must, never, always, refuse, or an imperative. Every other sentence is counted but not rowed. Each row carries five things: the rule, quoted or tightly paraphrased with its file and line at main HEAD; whether code enforces it, naming the refusal or check by file and symbol; whether it is still wanted, proposed by you, since the lead confirms that column; one disposition, one of delete as enforced, keep, merge into a named surviving row, or delete as obsolete; and a one-line reason. A row marked enforced names a test that drives the guarded action far enough to make the refusal or check fire. That test is run in the FOREGROUND and its log is cited by absolute path under the run directory; a rule with no such test is not marked enforced. The fragment states the file's total sentence count beside its row count, so the scope of binding is visible, and names the main HEAD sha it read at. Nothing in the skill files or the code is edited. The node writes only its own evidence fragment and figure directory. Figures are XML-safe and parsed with ElementTree. The manifest carries one landing: line.",
